cff-version: "1.2.0"

message: >-
  If you use the Research Software Ecosystem (RSEc) metadata commons
  in your work, please cite it using the metadata in this file.

title: "Research Software Ecosystem (RSEc) metadata commons"

type: dataset

abstract: >-
  The Research Software Ecosystem (RSEc) metadata commons is a public,
  version-controlled collection of metadata about research software.
  It aggregates and cross-links records from registries, package
  repositories, container infrastructures, workflow platforms, and
  benchmarking services. Source metadata are retained in their native
  or source-specific representations, while selected transformations
  and cross-links support discovery, interoperability, and reuse.

